{"id":"o-borschtbeltmuseum-org","claimKey":"8f37b9e010d1d6052f741f856ebeec4cbc5787289de27fbf8b9e34d3b4345972","title":"Borscht Belt Museum","cat":"play","art":"museum","area":"Ellenville, NY","metroId":"","src":"borschtbeltmuseum.org","specs":[],"options":[{"name":"Admission","detail":"Standard","price":15},{"name":"Guided Museum Tours","detail":"","price":null}],"services":[{"name":"Admission","desc":"The Borscht Belt enjoys a storied history as a haven for Jewish vacationers. During much of the 20th century, Jewish families from New York’s Lower East Side, Brooklyn, and the Bronx flocked to resorts and bungalow colonies surrounded by bucolic scenery to escape the city‘s stifling summers. Symbolizing assimilation and economic security, the resorts provided an abundance of familiar foods in generous spreads―often served with comedic entertainment―that fused Eastern European Jewish traditions with American influences. Many of the two-and-a-half million Eastern European Jews who migrated to the United States between 1880 and 1920 hoped to escape poverty. The arrivals- largely from Germany,","photo":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63291339ab29a04ec0e34fee/af6638cb-1d5a-47c1-9dc3-6c1daf6d06e3/Catskills+Romance+window+vinyl.jpg?format=2500w","variants":[{"label":"Standard","price":15,"optionIdx":0}]},{"name":"Guided Museum Tours","desc":null,"photo":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63291339ab29a04ec0e34fee/3f3f4f5d-5792-42cc-8142-3e3e78cd3d36/SPV-1511.jpg?format=2500w","variants":[{"label":"Standard","price":null,"optionIdx":1}]}],"includes":[],"addons":[],"gap":"Prices, hours and eligibility are not copied here yet. We will ask when you request.","cover":"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63291339ab29a04ec0e34fee/451255fd-da8e-45aa-ba6d-2407668c3d70/1950s-Borscht-Belt-Museum-Catskills-New-York-Photo-Archive.jpg?format=2500w","photos":["https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/63291339ab29a04ec0e34fee/451255fd-da8e-45aa-ba6d-